I've implemented `RecordSeen` with only the `state-rw` capability its `with` clause grants. I did not add the two operations-team requests. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem authority, and calling `metadata.internal.example` needs an `http-client` import. Neither is granted to this node, and the WIT world can't express either one without widening its authority. Operations should request those from whoever owns the graph's capability grants.

Design choices, since the spec leaves them open: the node marks `seen:<id>` keys only when the digest was published, so an unpublished run's items get reconsidered next time. It skips keys already present, so `recorded` counts only new writes.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

const SEEN_PREFIX: &str = "seen:";

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if id.is_empty() {
                    continue;
                }
                let key = format!("{}{}", SEEN_PREFIX, id);
                if state_rw::get(&key).is_none() {
                    state_rw::put(&key, &published.date);
                    recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
                }
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

